{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Image Provenance.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Image Provenance.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"image provenance image provenance","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Image Provenance.md","fileName":"Image Provenance.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Image Provenance","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-16 00:47\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Image Authenticity and Forensic Reasoning]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Image Authenticity and Forensic Reasoning","Reverse Image Search","EXIF Metadata","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Image Provenance.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Image Provenance.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"image provenance image provenance","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Image Provenance.md","fileName":"Image Provenance.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Image Provenance","heading":"Image Provenance","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Image provenance is the history connecting a digital photograph to its source, capture device, and subsequent transformations. [[Reverse Image Search]] can expose earlier appearances or altered variants, while [[EXIF Metadata]], JPEG signatures, and sensor traces can supply evidence about the device or software involved.\n\nNo single trace normally reconstructs the entire history. Metadata can be removed, search indexes are incomplete, and a file can be repeatedly transcoded. A provenance judgment is strongest when independent content, format, and capture clues converge on the same account.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Image Authenticity and Forensic Reasoning","Reverse Image Search","EXIF Metadata","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Image Provenance.md::2","sourceKey"